Section III-C, page 6:
  MAC performs an operation like GRF B += GRF A × BANK where SRC2 (GRF B) points to the same GRF register as DST. MAD does an operation like GRFA = BANK× SRF M + SRF A where SRC1 # and SRC2 # point to the same register index but in different register ﬁles (e.g., SRFM and SRF A, respectively).
